id: pm-vcs-op2c
title: Make every production TypeScript script part of exact coverage and add lint and duplication gates
description: "The current exact coverage gate reports 100/100/100 for its configured source set but omits accept-native-toon.ts and accept-stat-cache.ts; the package also has no explicit ESLint or jscpd release gate. Add behavior-driven instrumentation for every production script, a meaningful statement/branch/function/line contract where the runner supports it, parser-aware lint for the mandatory TypeScript rules, and a fail-closed duplicate-code gate without artificial tests or exclusions."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[7]: coverage,docstrings,duplication,lint,quality,release-blocker,typescript
created_at: "2026-08-07T13:01:18.790Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T07:40:13.313Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Every source and production script is instrumented by the repository coverage command; every supported coverage dimension is exactly 100%; ESLint enforces no explicit any, no inline or dynamic imports, erasable syntax, and repository conventions; jscpd or an equivalently strict duplicate-code detector runs fail-closed; release:check and prepublishOnly include all gates; tests are behavioral and do not use coverage ignores, artificial execution, or broad exclusions"
definition_of_ready: "Inventory all shipped and operational TypeScript files, inspect current compiler and Node coverage capabilities, and select maintained lint and duplication tooling compatible with TypeScript 7"
value: Makes the package's 100 percent claim literal across all production TypeScript
impact: "Prevents uninstrumented acceptance logic, duplicated implementation, and forbidden TypeScript constructs from bypassing release review"
outcome: One reproducible mandatory quality gate covers all production sources without cheats
why_now: The pm 2026.8.7 compatibility audit proved configured coverage is exact but discovered two acceptance scripts and lint/duplication enforcement outside that gate
parent: pm-vcs-tr2a
reviewer: maintainer
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-quality
release: Unreleased
severity: critical
environment: pm-vcs 2026.7.30 on Node 22 and TypeScript 7
repro_steps: "Inspect package.json coverageGate.sources and scripts; accept-native-toon.ts and accept-stat-cache.ts are absent, and no lint or duplicate-code script is defined"
component: quality/release
customer_impact: A release could currently satisfy configured coverage while regressions in operational acceptance scripts or duplicated/forbidden code remain undetected
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-o3jj,discovered_from,"2026-08-07T13:01:47.549Z",codex,pm-audit,asserted
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T10:08:37.713Z",codex-raw-coverage-repair,"Root verified frozen branch 70f42579086c59c695b151e65cda6459bbfa8e6f: 1240 passing tests, 53 production files at four-dimension C8 100%, LCOV 20707 lines/661 functions/5307 branches, SDK 2026.10.10 Node/Bun/CLI acceptance, 391 frozen fingerprints. Merged raw V8 still has two inherited zero-hit intervals: engine/repo.ts offsets 71425-71504 (createInstance cleanup failure, coverage ignore) and engine/serve.ts offsets 33366-33394 (request-body error wrapper). These invalidate a strict no-ignore/all-raw-positive claim. Reopening this existing owner under the no-artificial-execution/no-exclusion acceptance contract; preserve leases and original-error precedence. Related feature pm-vcs-8xis and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/97; root owns public review and checks."
  "2026-10-10T10:13:41.043Z",codex-raw-coverage-repair,"Inventory verified: the unchanged coverage command measures 53 root/engine/scripts TypeScript files; the only suppression was the createInstance cleanup c8 block. A real regular-file destination deterministically produces mkdir ENOTDIR followed by cleanup scandir ENOTDIR: the original syscall/path wins, the file survives, rollback stops at the first cleanup fault and the created branch remains recoverable. The shared-store lease releases and another instance links successfully; no cooperative race is claimed. Real socket EOF before Content-Length makes the request-body promise reject, settles the existing outcome hook and permits a subsequent advertisement. Both behavior tests pass on original source; the no-ignore policy assertion fails on original source. Negative source controls independently fail the mkdir-precedence and abort-settlement assertions; both fixed files restored byte-exact. Removed the sole suppression and replaced the one-use HTTP error wrapper with the real Node-typed rejection callback. SDK 2026.10.10/floor 2026.8.1 and coverage scope/thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-10T10:18:26.175Z","harness:codex","Orchestrator interruption preserves focused real-file/socket fixtures and source bytes. GitHub native workflows did not start because SDK pin/lock changes conflict with current main. Integrate main dependency updates, retain SDK2026.10.10 and independent8.1floor, regenerate lock and full self-host snapshot, then rerun unchanged all-source/raw/native/consumer gates. Prior70f4257 remains historical scopedC8 evidence with two raw gaps. No closure, force recovery, source gate approval or publication."
  "2026-10-10T10:20:35.511Z","harness:codex","Current main4324c968 integrated without discarding dependency changes: pm-ops2026.10.6 and pm-changelog2026.10.5 retained, exact development SDK2026.10.10/floor8.1 preserved, lock regenerated from main and reports zero dependency vulnerabilities. SDK-only package/lock conflicts are resolved. Real raw-coverage controls and every predecessor PM event retained; no accepted gate for this integrated tree until refreeze/selfhost regeneration/full unchanged source and consumer verification."
  "2026-10-10T10:26:16.714Z",codex-raw-coverage-repair,"Resumed after main integration at c2868ed with the same claim and all predecessor histories. Reviewed real regular-file cleanup and socket EOF contracts. The fixture now observes the actual native mkdir error and compares code/message/syscall/path instead of assuming ENOTDIR across platforms; it also verifies the distinct native readdir failure, unchanged notes, preserved recoverable branch, released lease and successful recovery. Removed the dummy callback. Installed Node supports withResolvers at runtime, but the configured ES2022 TypeScript library does not expose it, so the real synchronous Promise executor initializes the callback directly without changing compiler scope. Focused three tests, strict test compilation and unchanged quality checks pass. Current source-removal controls independently fail original-error precedence and aborted-body settlement; restored both production files byte-exact. No new production branches or exclusions. Final immutable full release/raw and SDK10 consumer proofs still pending."
  "2026-10-10T10:26:19.043Z",codex-raw-coverage-repair,"Freeze protocol: preserve main4324c968 and checkpoint a85850d as ancestors; retain SDK2026.10.10 with independent floor2026.8.1 plus main pm-ops2026.10.6 and pm-changelog2026.10.5. Release this claim unclosed before committing all source/test/docs/PM bytes, then regenerate selfhost.bundle and freeze its commit. Run the unchanged linked release:check with timeout3600; require all53 files at four100, positive raw executable ranges, matching Git/Istanbul/LCOV inventories and every tracked fingerprint, native TOON/strace/selfhost/identity/docs/changelog/audit/release acceptance plus current SDK10 built/npm-packed Node/native Bun/global CLI. No tracked edits after freeze; final immutable manifests and raw records are returned to the orchestrator. Inherited pending receipts are preserved without reconciliation; public checks and reviews remain with the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-10T10:40:08.032Z",codex-raw-coverage-repair,"Frozen candidate a75c2b5 completed 1243/1243 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations and all53 C8 source files at four100. Native TOON, installed CLI strace, selfhost byte identity, production audit, identity audit and dry-run packing passed. The complete release command failed at changelog:check: reopening this owner correctly removes its old closed-item changelog entry. This stale derived documentation was missed before the first freeze; the failed candidate and raw evidence are preserved externally. Regenerate CHANGELOG.md through the unchanged package command, verify the remaining release scripts, release this same claim unclosed, regenerate the bundle and freeze again. A second complete unchanged gate is required on the corrected snapshot; no push or full release claim from the failed candidate."
  "2026-10-10T10:42:41.289Z",codex-raw-coverage-repair,"Independent native audit of failed candidate a75c2b5 merged331 real V8 records: all53 production sources, 1154 functions and5311 ranges, zero unhit ranges. Installed Node Inspector types validate raw shapes; the installed stripTypeScriptTypes API verifies offset-preserving erasure and the exact appended sourceURL comment instead of guessing range bounds or excluding executable ranges. No type-only or unknown zero ranges were accepted as covered. The real cleanup catch is hit; the redundant HTTP wrapper is removed and the genuine abort fixture settles. CHANGELOG.md now matches the reopened owner through changelog:full/check; release date and publish-attestation scripts also pass. Every production file remains byte-exact to the reviewed/control-restored candidate. Preserve the failed receipt, release unclosed and refreeze all tracked documentation/PM/bundle bytes before the final unchanged complete gate."
  "2026-10-10T11:13:21.799Z",codex-publication-validation,"PR97 finding 4237410845 is confirmed in FileTransport push and publish: each ref starts a fresh closure walk. The installed source API already supports extra import publication roots, and the physical-root writer lease is synchronous and reentrant. Add bounded real SDK/filesystem tests for shared and distinct tips, unadvertised targets, corrupt/missing second targets, invalid names before mutation, force, stale CAS and receipt lifecycle. Batch every requested root under one lease without changing integrity or role-aware denial checks. Prior accepted 85e8a2e receipts remain historical only once source changes. Inspect the existing conservative malformed-encoding contract using ordinary fresh binary files after unrelated authorized erasure; do not weaken supported nested encoding refusal."
  "2026-10-10T11:18:21.511Z",codex-publication-validation,"Seven linked publication regressions pass with zero failures/skips. Real original operations measure three refs/two shared tips/five unique objects: push and publish each make five integrity reads under one native lock inode through refs and operation logging; old-source controls make sixteen and twelve reads. Restoring only both predecessor production modules makes the efficiency, invalid-name-before-arrival and unadvertised-second-root-before-arrival assertions fail with loaded modules; fixed bytes restored exactly. Corrupt and absent second targets, force, stale CAS/error classification and acceptedThisConnection reset remain covered. Existing integration passes 76/76 and expanded built/npm-packed Node/native Bun/global CLI consumers pass. Removed the obsolete single-target closure wrapper after its callers switched to the existing batch API; no integrity branch or coverage exclusion changed. Ordinary fresh binary staging passes after unrelated authorized erasure; malformed zlib-shaped and base64-wrapped candidates retain uninspectable_payload, while a retained encoded erased frame remains object_obliterated. This is the documented conservative supported representation contract, not a confirmed binary correctness defect."
  "2026-10-10T11:20:30.263Z",codex-publication-validation,"Freeze preparation: independent root PM receipt on the existing feature confirms the same conservative binary contract; retain that appended feature/history pair in the source snapshot. Own PM-linked publication and expanded SDK10 consumer commands pass; type/test compilation, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, dependency inventory, declared independent SDK floor, changelog regeneration/check, release-date and provenance checks pass. Only bundle and transport production bytes changed; all51 other executable sources and predecessor121 history prefixes remain unchanged. Health strict check passes with its inherited provenance advisory; validate succeeds with inherited metadata/resolution advisories, without reconciliation. Release this claim unclosed before committing all code/test/docs/PM bytes, regenerate selfhost.bundle and freeze its commit. Mandatory next gate is the unchanged linked release:check at timeout3600 plus fresh linked consumers, all53 per-file four100, positive actual native V8 ranges/sourceURL mappings, matching Git/Istanbul/LCOV inventories/counters and all immutable tracked hashes. Invalidate reports on any failed candidate; no push until every gate passes and the worktree is clean. Root owns final CI and public review; no closure, merge or publication."
  "2026-10-14T06:54:40.097Z",codex-agent,"Baseline origin/main already configures c8 --all --100 for 62 production TypeScript files, including all 12 scripts; existing jscpd 5.4.0 reports 62 sources and zero clones. Verify exact measurements before claiming an improvement. Reuse pm-ops 2026.10.6 ESLint and jscpd-5 APIs, keeping the production scan scope and zero threshold. The pinned artifact exports no coverage launcher and ships only the prepare template; retain c8 because it measures all four dimensions, then add behavioural omission and hostile-config controls. No pm-ops version bump."
  "2026-10-14T07:19:50.622Z",codex-agent,"Verified baseline: 1508/1508 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, all 62 production files and all 12 scripts at exact 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Canonical one-line-floor analysis found six short clones missed by the former five-line floor. Current implementation measures 63 production files (13 scripts), with zero clone pairs and zero duplicated lines; four new real-process controls pass. Revert proof: restoring only the previous lint config, only the previous coverage command, or only the refactored production modules makes its respective targeted behavioural test fail with exit 1; fixed bytes were independently restored exactly. Ordinary CLI guards replace three indexed no-op placeholders and are exercised by real self-host, identity and docstring subprocesses. Development glob dependency audit follow-up is pm-vcs-qfku; pm-ops remains pinned at 2026.10.6 and jscpd at 5.4.0."
  "2026-10-14T07:23:50.502Z",codex-agent,"Freeze receipt: linked real-process controls pass 4/4 with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Source and test compilation, canonical strict lint, zero duplicated lines across 63 files, and 350 documented declarations pass. Both exact isolated-identity release commands are linked. Preserve the failed context preflight receipt; tracker context completed successfully. Release the claim without closing, regenerate CHANGELOG.md after these writes, stage explicit source/test/tracker paths, regenerate and stage selfhost.bundle, then commit as SteveBot. Run npm and Bun release:check against that immutable head; publish their exact counts and per-script four-dimension coverage in the PR. No gate result is claimed for the final head before those commands finish."
  "2026-10-14T07:38:28.460Z",codex-agent,"Candidate 60f9729 passed all 1512 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, but failed coverage: statements/lines 96.86%, branches 95.58%, functions 97.96%. Do not treat that candidate as accepted. Raw records begin after the new nested fixture: c8 defaults tempDirectory to inherited NODE_V8_COVERAGE, and its normal cleanup deleted earlier parent records. Pin the repository coverage command to its project-local coverage/tmp directory; nested disposable projects then own separate collection paths. Add a real marker-file preservation assertion under an inherited parent coverage directory, rerun focused controls and the source-removal proof, regenerate changelog and bundle, refreeze, and rerun both complete isolated release gates. No source exclusions or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-14T07:40:12.479Z",codex-agent,"Collection isolation repair passes linked behavioural controls 4/4 with zero skips/failures. A real marker in an inherited parent coverage directory survives the fixed command; removing only --temp-directory=coverage/tmp causes c8 to delete that marker and makes the coverage control fail. Fixed bytes restored exactly. Source/test compilation, strict lint and zero-duplication checks still pass. Failed candidate receipts remain preserved; no artificial counters, coverage ignores, exclusions or weakened thresholds were introduced. Release unclosed, regenerate changelog and self-host bundle, commit the repair, then rerun both full release commands on that exact immutable head."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T00:41:47.815Z","harness:codex","The package remains intentionally unpublished: audit:identities still rejects exactly one known non-public historical address,independently of these clean code-quality gates."
  "2026-08-08T00:42:45.025Z","harness:codex",The default pm health --strict-exit reproduced the known unbraind/pm-cli#928 silent provider-refresh hang and was stopped after four minutes; CI now uses the documented --check-only mode and the read-only strict health gate completes promptly.
  "2026-08-08T00:54:56.864Z","harness:codex",PR #20 Windows Node 22 and 26 logs proved execFileSync cannot launch a bare pm name backed by npm pm.CMD. Discovery now returns the exact validated shim path and uses the Windows shell only at that validated boundary; POSIX remains direct execution.
  "2026-08-08T01:00:28.691Z","harness:codex","Accepted all three remaining CodeRabbit findings on the first review head: parser failure is tracked independently of the thrown value; equal-content reconciliation no longer leaks copiedFrom across the selected FileId; and the real strace success path runs only on a Linux host with strace available. Added reversed-provenance behavior coverage."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T00:41:47.815Z","harness:codex",An explicit source allowlist can report perfect coverage while omitting operational scripts. c8 --all makes absence measurable; behavior-driven failure fixtures also exposed unreachable defensive branches that were better simplified.
